// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1, part (a) (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P8): a global text aliased into a global
// record's text field. Originally (4e): the select-LHS store rule
// disqualified only the FIELD NAME on a non-fresh store, never the
// record's own base -- `cl_free_globals` still recursed into `p8GRec`'s
// fields, freeing `body` (== `p8Gt`'s handle, after the store), then
// separately froze `p8Gt` itself: SIGSEGV. The fix disqualifies the BASE
// identifier (`p8GRec`) too -- still true today, unchanged by ARC Task 4:
// `cl_free_globals` stays empty, skipping `p8GRec` entirely (records are
// Task 7's still-unmigrated slot class; globals cleanup is Task 6's).
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p8GRec.body = p8Gt` is a
// SELECT-LHS store -- `lowAssign`'s generic fallthrough doesn't
// distinguish a record field from a window var, so this ALSO routes
// through `lowCountedStore` (an early, incidental win Task 7 will
// formalize, not a bug: retaining a field store can only ever be a leak
// if unbalanced, never a UAF). Confirmed against the emitted C:
// `rt_text_retain(cv_p8Gt); rt_text_release((cv_p8GRec).cv_body);
// (cv_p8GRec).cv_body = cv_p8Gt;` -- `p8ProbeNote`'s original `body = "hi"`
// default handle is properly freed now (no longer the permanent
// orphan-on-overwrite this comment used to describe), and `p8Gt` is
// retained into the field. Expected strict-mode leak count: 2 (see
// ../p8_rec_field.leaks, dropped from 4) -- `p8Gt`'s "keep" text only
// (struct box + data handle, 2 blocks; rc==2 after the retain, shared with
// `p8GRec.body`, counted once) -- never released, since neither global
// cleanup (Task 6) nor a record field release-walk (Task 7) exist yet. Not
// a bug -- both are explicitly out of this task's scope.

record p8ProbeNote {
    body: text = "hi"
}

var p8Gt: text = "keep"
var p8GRec: p8ProbeNote

func runP8RecField() {
    p8GRec.body = p8Gt
    alert("p8 done")
}
